A||||7||Dan010||Oil pressure gauge||||1||
Z||000000||Dan010||10-05-2001||11:16 PM||||Hi, new here, just bought a 86 gt, great car<BR> new problem, oil pressure gauge now flat<BR>lines to the right, before this happened,<BR>worked some what, what might be the fix?<BR>Also, service engine light comes on once in <BR>a while, tomarrow will do test, but any ideas<BR> Great site!!!!!!!!!<BR>Dan||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||10-05-2001||11:38 PM||||If the oil pressure gauge goes full pressure when the ignition is ON, but reads normal when engine is running, that is acceptable.  If it is pegged at all times, check the oil pressure sender connector and wiring for any wires that might be shorting out to ground.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Pike||10-05-2001||11:42 PM||||I'm new here also....but I've heard something about this problem. The gauge is on a circuit that drives the needle full over during starting. The fix is to drill a small hole and insert (glue) a small wire stop for the needle. Without it, eventually the needle will peg over all the way and stick. If your sure you have oil pressure...the next best thing is a replacement gauge.<BR>Regards,<BR>Pike||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroJoe||10-06-2001||12:06 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Pike:<BR><B>I'm new here also....but I've heard something about this problem. The gauge is on a circuit that drives the needle full over during starting. The fix is to drill a small hole and insert (glue) a small wire stop for the needle. Without it, eventually the needle will peg over all the way and stick. If your sure you have oil pressure...the next best thing is a replacement gauge.<BR>Regards,<BR>Pike</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The oil pressure gauge isn't wired to do that, it is the water temperature.  There is more of a problem with the gauge in the backlit (V6) clusters with the needle sticking than with the clusters in the 4 banger.  Yes, they both will to the peggy thing, but the backlit one has more of a chance of getting stuck for some reason.<P>Every once and a while my oil pressure will be pegged when I turn the car on, but then go back to normal once the engine is started.  This happened with both gauges I had, original coupe gauges and then when I went to the backlit gauges and aux cluster.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Old Lar||10-06-2001||04:47 AM||||When the oil pressure gauge pegs and stays there it is a sign that the oil sender unit  failing.(or wiring from the oil sender unit). I'm on my 3rd one in my 87 and 88 GTs.  Not the greatest designed piece of equipment, but a relatively cheap and easy fix.<P>The 87 unit is different from the 88.||||reg||1
Z||000005||btoth||10-06-2001||10:45 AM||||Just be glad it's not going to the left.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  j/k||||reg||6
Z||000006||sqoach||10-06-2001||10:59 AM||||What if it bounces around all over the place? After a while, it'll at least go to normal, but it'll still bounce around at times, usually when I'm stopping/idling.<P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">            <BR>^^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^^<BR><LI><FONT SIZE="1">84 SE (FOR SALE)*SOLD*<BR><LI>85 Coupe (parts car)($50)*sale pending*<BR><LI>86 SC</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Dan010||10-06-2001||11:44 AM||||Thanks for all your help,<BR>will give it a try to day to see what it is<BR>Thank again<BR>Dan<BR>||||reg||1
